  "FLINK-31665": {
    "jira_id": "FLINK-31665",
    "issue_type": "Improvement",
    "resolution": "Fixed",
    "title": "Add ARRAY_CONCAT supported in SQL & Table API",
    "description": "This is an implementation of ARRAY_CONCEPT\r\n\r\nThe array_concat() function concatenates at least one array, creating an array that contains all the elements in the first array followed by all the elements in the second array ... followed by all the elements in the n array.\r\nh3. Brief change log\r\n\r\nARRAY_CONCAT for Table API and SQL\r\n\r\nSyntax:\r\n{code:java}\r\nARRAY_CONCAT(arr1, tail...){code}\r\n\r\nArguments:\r\narray: at least one ARRAY to be handled.\r\n\r\nReturns:\r\nThe function returns NULL if any input argument is NULL.\r\n\r\nExamples:\r\n{code:java}\r\nFlink SQL> SELECT array_concat(array[1, 2, 3, null, 3], array[3], array[5]); [1, 2, 3, null, 3, 3]{code}\r\nsee also:\r\nGoogle Cloud BigQuery: [https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/standard-sql/array_functions#array_concat]",
    "commits": [
      {
        "sha": "eedabdc4e4d292517e844d7cb9ff040575598e78",
        "message": "[FLINK-31665] [table] Add ARRAY_CONCAT function",
        "author": "hanyuzheng7",
        "date": "2023-06-05T17:22:51Z",
        "files": [
